    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the sole `POST /api/owners` handler):\n\n1. Added a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n   ```\n\n2. Emitted an audit line immediately after a successful `saveOwner`, carrying the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`:\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe log fires only on the success path (after all validation/quota rules and the persist), and uses the values as actually assigned to the entity, so they match what `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns. The acceptance test `coreLogsAuditOnCreate` and the whole suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
